{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"capability-evolver-pro","displayName":"Capability Evolver","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/kennyzir/skills/capability-evolver-pro","publisherHandle":"kennyzir","publisherDisplayName":"claw0x","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/kennyzir","version":"1.0.2","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774342319973,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/capability-evolver-pro/card?ownerHandle=kennyzir&version=1.0.2","sha256":"ff897311aee6b30323e7401dab7f3eaf4cf27afc870a3fb9110835f212b47552","size":1676,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"26558dd471daa995ca67c340c469ed345f408f14a97af79079e021cf5cac6677","bundleFingerprints":["6f6c67e0ac1dbe10d6913698609948c29973e2ede7799906fe5102ee9b32a622","3724dd7057d97c2b82bc784db383af5a0cffa2a3b606cf54d11da934a36576d7"],"files":[{"path":"handler.ts","size":13361,"sha256":"aabe6e2346141dc3765dc0fd5d478c618743cb77d74e7968dfe5fe077b58d207","contentType":"video/vnd.dlna.mpeg-tts"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":19119,"sha256":"41cf3470c4f5b5426a19d551d2af5d92b92862517db81dac5d512bbd145c512a","contentType":null}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a local log-analysis skill with no evident network, filesystem mutation, credential access, or persistence, though users should bound log input size.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789433408245,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unenforced Log-Volume Limit Enables Resource Exhaustion"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"handler.ts"},"region":{"startLine":95,"endLine":98}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"70e900f05fdce3da"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `handler.ts:95-98`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Missing input-size validation leading to denial of service  \n**Risk Level**: Medium  \n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```typescript\nif ((input.action === 'analyze' || input.action === 'evolve') &&\n    (!input.logs || !Array.isArray(input.logs) || input.logs.length === 0)) {\n  errors.push('\"logs\" array is required for analyze/evolve actions');\n}\n```\n\nThe Skill separately advertises a maximum of 10,000 log entries, but this value is informational and is not applied during validation:\n\n```typescript\nlimits: {\n  max_logs_per_request: 10000,\n  max_patterns_returned: 50,\n  max_recommendations: 20,\n},\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe request validator only verifies that `logs` is a non-empty array for the `analyze` and `evolve` actions. It does not enforce the advertised `max_logs_per_request` limit or any maximum request size.\n\nAccepted logs are processed synchronously through multiple full-array operations, including iteration, filtering, mapping, reduction, and sorting. The analysis also constructs maps and sets from attacker-controlled messages and contexts. The `evolve` action invokes the same analysis routine before generating recommendations.\n\nConsequently, an untrusted caller can provide an extremely large log array that consumes excessive CPU and heap memory. Returning only 50 patterns does not mitigate the issue because the complete input is processed and intermediate collections are created before the result is truncated.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker or untrusted integration invokes the Skill with the `analyze` or `evolve` action.\n2. The request contains a valid but extremely large `logs` array, substantially exceeding the documented 10,000-entry limit.\n3. Validation accepts the request because it only checks whether the array exists and is non-empty.\n4. The Skill synchronously iterates over the entire array and creates intermediate maps, filtered arrays, sets, and sorted collections.\n5. CPU time and memory usage increase until the agent becomes unresponsive, the request times out, or the runtime terminates due to memory exhaustion.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation can cause denial of service within the process executing the Skill. This can delay or terminate other agent operations sharing the same runtime and may trigger container or worker restarts.\n\nThe vulnerability does not provide command execution, filesystem access, network access, credential access, persistence, or privilege escalation. Its demonstrated scope is resource exhaustion within the hosting process and any co-located workloads affected by that process becoming unavailable.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Enforce the advertised limit directly in `validateRequest`:\n\n```typescript\nconst MAX_LOGS_PER_REQUEST = 10_000;\n\nif (\n  (input.action === 'analyze' || input.action === 'evolve') &&\n  Array.isArray(input.logs) &&\n  input.logs.length > MAX_LOGS_PER_REQUEST\n) {\n  errors.push(`\"logs\" must contain at most ${MAX_LOGS_PER_REQUEST} entries`);\n}\n```\n\n2. Define the limit once and reuse the same constant in both validation and `handleStatus` to prevent documentation and implementation from diverging.\n3. Validate every log entry, including the types and maximum lengths of `timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `context`, and `stack`.\n4. Apply an overall serialized request-size limit at the API or agent boundary.\n5. Consider processing large permitted inputs in bounded batches or through streaming logic rather than constructing multiple full-size intermediate arrays.\n6. Configure runtime memory, execution-time, and concurrency limits as defense-in-depth controls.\n7. Add tests confirming that arrays of 10,001 or more entries are rejected before analysis begins.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789433323.5341141,"endTime":1789433379.0704238}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"Capability Evolver","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v570nh21tsec2h4me2tjza50bs8eeck5-pnaDnf/clawscan-skillspector-2643656817/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T00:48:42.069014+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":14,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":524,"executable":false,"size_bytes":19119,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"handler.ts","type":"typescript","lines":358,"executable":true,"size_bytes":13361,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-a453e6b1c1414aa79566ba1de7138e39","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":382,"end_line":382},"finding":null,"explanation":"The 'When to Use' section lists trigger examples such as 'what's failing', 'improve my agent', and 'check system health', which are broad phrases that could arise in many ordinary conversations. The file does not provide exclusion conditions or tighter context boundaries there, increasing the risk of unintended invocation.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger guidance to explicit capability-evolver intents, such as requests to analyze structured runtime logs or generate log-based evolution proposals. Add negative examples or scope limits clarifying that general debugging or generic improvement requests should not trigger the skill unless logs or health-analysis context are present.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":382,"end_line":382}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-e562cfa225134e478f910cc431cbe7e1","category":null,"pattern":null,"